        "Weigh every child in kilograms on admission and weekly, write it on the chart, estimate only in emergencies ((age + 4) × 2; (months ÷ 2) + 4); dose = mg/kg × kg (per dose or per day — read which), volume = desired ÷ stock × volume in one unit, never exceed the adult maximum, check the decimal, ask whether it makes sense.",
        "The ten-fold error is the paediatric error: defend against it with an independent second calculation for every calculated dose and high-alert drug, micrograms and units written in full, leading zeros and no trailing zeros, read-back of verbal orders with the weight, the paediatric dilution chart, labelled syringes and oral syringes that cannot connect to a line.",
        "Core doses: paracetamol 10–15 mg/kg 4–6-hourly (max 4 doses/day); ibuprofen 5–10 mg/kg; amoxicillin 40 mg/kg twice daily for pneumonia; ampicillin 50 mg/kg 6-hourly; gentamicin 7.5 mg/kg once daily (5 mg/kg neonate); ceftriaxone 50–100 mg/kg; artesunate 3 mg/kg under 20 kg (rectal 10 mg/kg); AL by weight band; salbutamol 2–10 puffs by spacer; prednisolone 1–2 mg/kg; rectal diazepam 0.5 mg/kg; adrenaline 1:1,000 IM 0.01 mL/kg for anaphylaxis and 1:10,000 0.1 mL/kg for arrest; zinc 10/20 mg; vitamin A 50,000/100,000/200,000 IU; oral morphine 0.1–0.2 mg/kg 4-hourly with a laxative.",
        "Oral medicines go by oral syringe slowly into the cheek of a semi-upright child, never flat, crying or mixed into a full feed; intramuscular injections go into the anterolateral thigh in infants (max 1 mL), the deltoid for small volumes from one to two years, never the dorsogluteal site; intravenous drugs are diluted to the chart, given over the stated time through a visible, checked site with a burette or pump; rectal diazepam when there is no vein; inhalers always through a spacer.",
        "Teach the caregiver by demonstration with her own bottle and syringe, watch her give the first dose, write the dose in millilitres and the times in words or pictures, explain the whole course, the vomited or missed dose, side effects, storage and no added herbal remedies, and confirm by teach-back.",
