        "Children's fluids are prescribed by weight, delivered through a burette holding no more than one to two hours' volume or a pump, and checked against a fluid balance chart and a daily weight; a child's requirement per kilogram is two to three times an adult's and her reserves are tiny.",
        "Maintenance by Holliday–Segar is 100 mL/kg for the first 10 kg, 50 mL/kg for the next 10 and 20 mL/kg thereafter per day (4-2-1 mL/kg/h), reduced to two-thirds in meningitis, pneumonia, head injury, heart and renal failure and after surgery; newborns start at 60 mL/kg/day of 10 % dextrose rising about 20 mL/kg/day to 150.",
